# A Mudlet package archive is a zip, and a map file is a binary blob. Git's
# content sniffing gets this right for most of them, but not for the busted
# fixture that is deliberately *not* a zip — that one looks like text, and a
# CRLF checkout on Windows would rewrite the very bytes the fixture exists to
# hand the installer. The sync scripts round-trip these byte-for-byte; say so
# here too, or git undoes that on the way out of the repo.
*.mpackage binary
*.dat binary
